This directory contains work from two different places. They are listed
separately because the terms are not the same.


1. THE TEMPLATE
---------------
style.tex, slides.tex, demo.tex, check.sh, README.md

    Copyright the contributors to this repository.
    Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

    You may copy, adapt and redistribute this, including commercially,
    provided you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate
    whether you made changes.

    There is no upstream theme to credit here. The beamer themes underneath —
    Madrid, miniframes, circles — ship with beamer itself and carry beamer's
    own licence; using them creates no obligation. Everything above them, the
    palette and its derivations, the seven named blocks, the title page and
    the SWOT grid, was written for this deck.


2. THE COVER PHOTOGRAPH
-----------------------
figures/background.png

    A photograph taken by the author, edited with a generative tool into the
    watercolour treatment you see. Same CC BY 4.0 terms as the rest.

    It is here because a template with no cover image cannot be judged: the
    title box was designed against a photograph and looks wrong on a flat
    ground. Replace it with your own and nothing else needs changing —
    \slateBackground is one line in style.tex, and the watermark on every
    other slide reads from the same file.

    If you do replace it, look at two things. The title box is a pale
    gradient, so it disappears over a pale sky; and the watermark sits at
    6.7%, which was set against an image of this lightness.


3. THE LOGO PLACEHOLDER
-----------------------
figures/logo.png

    A placeholder, not a mark. No institution's logo ships with this template.
    A logo is its owner's trademark and the licence above does not extend to
    it; putting one in a public repository is not something a CC licence can
    make lawful. Replace the file locally and keep it out of the history.
